00:03:12.710 --> 00:03:16.420
We are going to need a more elaborate strategy.

00:03:16.710 --> 00:03:19.330
<b>Plan for Peace Throughout the World, Vol. 1</b>

00:03:19.580 --> 00:03:24.000
And so, I hereby commence the first
100,000 Likes Project conference.

00:03:24.000 --> 00:03:25.710
Let's do this!

00:03:25.710 --> 00:03:28.250
So, is this guy always dressed like that?

00:03:28.250 --> 00:03:29.250
Yep.

00:03:29.460 --> 00:03:31.000
Ah, excuse me for a sec.

00:03:31.460 --> 00:03:35.040
Well then, please turn to page four in your handouts.

00:03:35.630 --> 00:03:38.830
These are the details of the 100,000 Likes Project,

00:03:37.330 --> 00:03:41.290
<b>The post must be made from the candidate's</b>

00:03:37.330 --> 00:03:41.290
<b>own social media account.</b>

00:03:38.830 --> 00:03:41.540
on which the right to appear at the
major festival Summer Sonia hinges.

00:03:41.290 --> 00:03:49.250
<b>The 100,000 likes must be on a single post</b>

00:03:41.290 --> 00:03:49.250
<b>and not the sum of multiple posts.</b>

00:03:41.540 --> 00:03:44.830
"The post must be made from the
candidate's own social media account."

00:03:45.080 --> 00:03:49.540
"The 100,000 likes must be on a single post
and not the sum of multiple posts."

00:03:49.250 --> 00:03:53.330
<b>The content of the post will be left</b>

00:03:49.250 --> 00:03:53.330
<b>to the candidate's discretion.</b>

00:03:49.540 --> 00:03:53.330
"The content of the post will be left
to the candidate's discretion."

00:03:53.500 --> 00:03:55.210
We have twenty days until the deadline.

00:03:55.420 --> 00:03:58.000
Multiple artists have entered the competition,

00:03:58.000 --> 00:04:03.290
and the right to perform at Summer Sonia will be
awarded to whoever first gets 100,000 likes.

00:04:00.420 --> 00:04:03.460
<b>Likes received!!</b>

00:04:00.420 --> 00:04:03.460
<b>GUARANTEED SLOT</b>

00:04:03.630 --> 00:04:07.040
Incidentally, these three groups are
currently looking the strongest.

00:04:07.540 --> 00:04:12.830
Ice Born, a duo that is popular for their songs
that fuse club music with J-pop.

00:04:12.830 --> 00:04:15.830
Salesio Teikoku, a bona-fide rock band.

00:04:15.460 --> 00:04:19.580
<b>Salesio</b>

00:04:15.460 --> 00:04:19.580
<b>Teikoku</b>

00:04:15.830 --> 00:04:19.580
Finally, there's the girl band Azalea,
who are popular with young folks.

00:04:19.750 --> 00:04:23.040
Uh-oh, Ice Born already has a post with 60,000 likes!

00:04:23.420 --> 00:04:25.960
And even second-place Salesio Teikoku
has gotten 40,000.

00:04:26.290 --> 00:04:27.880
We've really gotten off to a late start.

00:04:28.040 --> 00:04:30.080
I've gotta hurry and post something!

00:04:30.170 --> 00:04:31.250
Hold on, please.

00:04:31.250 --> 00:04:32.250
But!

00:04:32.250 --> 00:04:34.500
The time for that has not yet come.

00:04:34.920 --> 00:04:36.880
The heavens, time, and man:

00:04:37.040 --> 00:04:40.080
When taking action, one must sense
when opportunity presents itself.

00:04:40.250 --> 00:04:43.420
Besides, Ice Born has already peaked.

00:04:43.580 --> 00:04:44.580
Huh?

00:04:45.000 --> 00:04:48.630
My analysis of the likes trend over the last two weeks

00:04:48.630 --> 00:04:51.210
shows that the numbers have leveled off
in the past five days.

00:04:51.210 --> 00:04:54.750
In short, people have already tired
of their publicity campaign.

00:04:55.040 --> 00:04:57.670
Posting so much out of the gate has
now become detrimental.

00:04:58.080 --> 00:05:01.710
Likewise, second-place Salesio Teikoku
has reached their upper limit.

00:04:58.250 --> 00:05:04.960
<b>Salesio</b>

00:04:58.250 --> 00:05:04.960
<b>Teikoku</b>

00:05:01.710 --> 00:05:04.960
It seems they couldn't sufficiently expand
beyond their core fanbase.

00:05:05.380 --> 00:05:06.580
So...

00:05:06.710 --> 00:05:08.880
the group we really have to watch out for is...

00:05:10.130 --> 00:05:12.750
Azalea, who currently sit in third.

00:05:15.040 --> 00:05:16.290
"Azalea"?

00:05:16.630 --> 00:05:20.380
Their vocalist, Nanami Kuon,
is a superbly talented singer.

00:05:20.380 --> 00:05:22.960
However, that's not our biggest cause for concern.

00:05:23.790 --> 00:05:28.750
You see, the girls are backed by Key Time,
a major agency.

00:05:28.750 --> 00:05:30.000
Key Time?!

00:05:30.460 --> 00:05:32.880
The one that's known to do whatever it takes to sell?

00:05:32.880 --> 00:05:34.290
THAT Key Time?

00:05:34.750 --> 00:05:38.420
Someone I know had their contract
unilaterally terminated by them.

00:05:38.420 --> 00:05:40.130
Haven't heard a good word about 'em.

00:05:40.290 --> 00:05:44.750
In any case, they possess several hundred times
our publicity funds and human resources.

00:05:44.750 --> 00:05:49.210
If we don't do something about those girls,
there is no viable path to Summer Sonia.

00:05:49.460 --> 00:05:51.540
Then, we better get crackin' right away.

00:05:51.790 --> 00:05:53.250
When're you planning to make a move?!

00:05:53.460 --> 00:05:59.080
The day to outflank them and make a post that
racks up 100,000 likes as fast as possible is...

00:06:00.040 --> 00:06:01.750
When is it?

00:06:02.790 --> 00:06:04.130
Exactly...

00:06:04.130 --> 00:06:05.670
three days before the deadline.

00:06:07.210 --> 00:06:08.420
Just three days?!

00:06:08.420 --> 00:06:17.000
<b>X Day</b>

00:06:08.670 --> 00:06:10.710
We shall call this "X Day."

00:06:10.710 --> 00:06:12.880
Aren't you cutting it a bit too close?!

00:06:12.880 --> 00:06:15.420
Besides, how are you even planning
to get 100,000 likes?

00:06:15.420 --> 00:06:16.790
Yeah!
Excuse me.<b></b>

00:06:17.080 --> 00:06:19.130
Naturally, I do have a plan.

00:06:19.330 --> 00:06:22.380
But before we get to that, Kabetaijin...

00:06:23.330 --> 00:06:26.750
please have a proper showdown
with Sekitoba Kung Fu.

00:06:26.920 --> 00:06:27.920
Huh?!

00:06:27.920 --> 00:06:29.420
Who's Sekitoba?

00:06:29.420 --> 00:06:31.880
He was next to you during the rap battle, you know?

00:06:31.880 --> 00:06:34.670
Oh, that guy who explained everything!

00:06:35.210 --> 00:06:39.830
He's challenged you to a rematch at that
rap battle competition just before X Day, right?

00:06:39.830 --> 00:06:41.880
Well, yeah, he did...

00:06:41.880 --> 00:06:43.210
Wait, how'd you know that?

00:06:43.380 --> 00:06:48.130
If you're preoccupied, you won't be able
to exhibit your best performance.

00:06:48.380 --> 00:06:49.540
It will be all right.

00:06:49.540 --> 00:06:52.790
The Kabe now standing before me
can reach still further heights.

00:06:53.210 --> 00:06:54.420
That's right!

00:06:54.540 --> 00:06:55.790
Let's both do our best!

00:06:58.170 --> 00:07:00.880
<b>Confidential</b>

00:06:58.170 --> 00:07:00.880
<b>The Path to Success in the</b>

00:06:58.170 --> 00:07:00.880
<b>100,000 Likes Project</b>

00:06:58.170 --> 00:07:00.880
<b>Zhuge Kongming</b>

00:06:58.750 --> 00:07:00.880
So, the essence of this stratagem...

00:07:01.130 --> 00:07:03.630
relies on Eiko's singing.

00:07:04.130 --> 00:07:05.710
All right! Got it!

00:07:07.960 --> 00:07:10.210
And the song we will pin our hopes on is...

00:07:10.880 --> 00:07:12.580
<b>Roppongi</b>

00:07:10.880 --> 00:07:12.580
<b>Udon Shop (Working Title)</b>

00:07:10.880 --> 00:07:12.580
<b>Lyrics/Music EIKO</b>

00:07:11.580 --> 00:07:14.500
Kurikaesu every day
Repeating every day<b></b>

00:07:14.960 --> 00:07:18.000
Naku koto mo wasure
Forgetting even to cry<b></b>

00:07:14.960 --> 00:07:16.420
When'd you make that?

00:07:16.420 --> 00:07:19.290
B-but I've only made a demo recording so far!

00:07:18.500 --> 00:07:19.500
Iro...
Stripped...<b></b>

00:07:19.500 --> 00:07:21.710
<b>Roppongi</b>

00:07:19.500 --> 00:07:21.710
<b>Udon Shop (Working Title)</b>

00:07:19.960 --> 00:07:22.330
The deadline's in two weeks and change...

00:07:22.710 --> 00:07:26.670
Think I can turn it into a song that
gets 100,000 likes by then?

00:07:26.920 --> 00:07:30.920
I've already secured a studio and virtuoso arranger.

00:07:31.250 --> 00:07:33.580
Above all, so long as we have Kabetaijin,

00:07:33.580 --> 00:07:36.580
who pierces through to the truth and
stirs the hearts of his audience,

00:07:36.580 --> 00:07:41.710
together with Eiko's singing, which resonates in
the soul and deeply moves all who hear it...

00:07:42.130 --> 00:07:45.880
garnering 100,000 likes will be easier
than turning over a fan.

00:07:46.130 --> 00:07:47.130
I shall name this:

00:07:46.830 --> 00:07:51.250
<b>Plan for Peace Throughout the World</b>

00:07:52.170 --> 00:07:54.960
"Plan for Peace Throughout the World, Volume 1."

00:07:57.000 --> 00:08:00.460
We shall surely make Eiko's singing
resound throughout the world

00:08:00.460 --> 00:08:03.380
and save the hearts and minds of the lost populace!

00:08:04.130 --> 00:08:05.330
"Populace"?

00:08:05.710 --> 00:08:07.000
Populace...

00:08:07.790 --> 00:08:10.630
Got it! I'll give it my best!

00:08:10.830 --> 00:08:14.170
Hmm, guess I can't do battle
if I don't clear my head first.

00:08:16.330 --> 00:08:19.830
All right! I'm gonna conjure up
some vibes for the showdown!

00:08:19.830 --> 00:08:23.040
Kongming, you can count on me
to really polish this song!

00:08:23.630 --> 00:08:24.960
They sure show promise.

00:08:24.960 --> 00:08:25.960
Indeed.

00:08:26.540 --> 00:08:28.710
They must evolve.

00:08:29.040 --> 00:08:30.420
As must we.

00:08:33.210 --> 00:08:34.500
Guitar, check.

00:08:34.710 --> 00:08:35.880
Voice, check.

00:08:36.080 --> 00:08:37.290
Physical condition, check.

00:08:37.630 --> 00:08:39.130
I'm all set to go!

00:08:40.330 --> 00:08:42.170
Aw, I sure am nervous.

00:08:42.170 --> 00:08:45.790
This is my first time ever doing a studio recording.

00:08:46.380 --> 00:08:47.630
Ah, that's right!

00:08:50.290 --> 00:08:51.290
Eiko...

00:08:51.830 --> 00:08:54.630
I'm unable to accompany you to your recording session,

00:08:54.630 --> 00:08:56.790
but please take these.

00:08:58.920 --> 00:09:00.830
What is this? Can I open it?

00:09:01.130 --> 00:09:04.630
No, please open it only if you find
yourself feeling anxious.

00:09:04.830 --> 00:09:06.630
I believe it will be of service.

00:09:06.920 --> 00:09:10.170
I've numbered them, so please use them accordingly.

00:09:10.960 --> 00:09:12.170
Got it!

00:09:12.380 --> 00:09:15.960
Now, please do remember to open them in order.

00:09:16.920 --> 00:09:18.580
Well, that's what he told me.

00:09:19.460 --> 00:09:21.750
Only if I get anxious, hmm...

00:09:23.420 --> 00:09:24.630
Here goes!

00:09:25.130 --> 00:09:29.960
<b>You should buy two,</b>

00:09:25.130 --> 00:09:29.960
<b>jumbo value-size</b>

00:09:25.130 --> 00:09:29.960
<b>Puri Puddings.</b>

00:09:25.670 --> 00:09:29.460
One: "You should buy two,
jumbo value-size Puri Puddings."

00:09:29.710 --> 00:09:30.710
Also, let's see...

00:09:29.960 --> 00:09:33.500
<b>Application for Permission for Public Road Usage</b>

00:09:29.960 --> 00:09:33.500
<b>Name    Eiko Tsukimi</b>

00:09:29.960 --> 00:09:33.500
<b>Intended Usage of Road                 Live performance</b>

00:09:29.960 --> 00:09:33.500
<b>Place or Section                 Shibuya Hachiko Square thru Center Gai</b>

00:09:30.710 --> 00:09:33.290
Two: A public-road-usage permit.

00:09:34.040 --> 00:09:37.960
Three: A ticket for the observation deck
at Shibuya Sky Square.

00:09:39.750 --> 00:09:41.960
Uh-oh, dunno what this all means.

00:09:42.500 --> 00:09:44.290
Well, I'll start with the pudding.

00:09:43.460 --> 00:09:45.170
<b>Select-Ingredients Bento Fair</b>

00:09:45.710 --> 00:09:47.420
Thank you!

00:09:48.170 --> 00:09:51.170
<i>I've let Sekitoba know that I'm in.</i>

00:09:52.130 --> 00:09:54.250
I'll have a yakisoba bread and cola, okay?

00:09:54.250 --> 00:09:55.460
Then, same for me too.

00:09:55.460 --> 00:09:57.040
B-but I treated you guys yesterday.

00:09:57.040 --> 00:09:58.250
Don't you talk back to us, Sato.

00:09:58.250 --> 00:09:59.790
C-cut that out.
Don't you talk back to us, Sato.<b></b>

00:09:59.790 --> 00:10:01.830
C'mon, hurry and get our stuff.

00:10:01.830 --> 00:10:06.500
You should be grateful we hang out
with a ordinary Joe like you.

00:10:06.500 --> 00:10:08.040
Get your butt in the store already!

00:10:10.040 --> 00:10:12.750
So he's back in the game now, you know, Kabe?

00:10:12.750 --> 00:10:15.130
He's got technique, but that's all.

00:10:15.130 --> 00:10:17.420
It was shocking to see his rap fall flat.

00:10:17.420 --> 00:10:19.630
His freestyle record must've been a fluke.

00:10:19.630 --> 00:10:20.630
Yeah, man.

00:10:20.630 --> 00:10:23.040
It's lame when a gloomy average Joe tries to look cool.

00:10:24.670 --> 00:10:28.500
Swallows and sparrows cannot comprehend
the aspirations of phoenixes and swans.

00:10:28.750 --> 00:10:32.630
Small birds don't understand the feelings
of large birds that soar high in the sky.

00:10:32.630 --> 00:10:33.830
What the hell, punk?!

00:10:33.830 --> 00:10:36.790
Is there a problem, sir?

00:10:37.830 --> 00:10:39.920
H-hey, just forget it, man.

00:10:44.290 --> 00:10:47.080
That line's from your war of words
before Battle of the Red Cliffs!

00:10:48.130 --> 00:10:50.210
Are you alright, Kabe?

00:10:50.540 --> 00:10:52.250
Huh? Whaddaya mean?

00:10:52.790 --> 00:10:55.380
I've got inner steel these days, you know!

00:10:55.540 --> 00:10:58.170
Tell me, what is true strength?

00:10:58.880 --> 00:11:01.920
Uh, brawn, or something?

00:11:02.210 --> 00:11:05.210
Can one really save the people with that?

00:11:05.210 --> 00:11:06.210
Huh?

00:11:06.540 --> 00:11:10.710
Apparent strength is not, in fact, true strength.

00:11:18.080 --> 00:11:19.830
E-excuse me...

00:11:19.830 --> 00:11:20.830
Huh?

00:11:22.040 --> 00:11:23.500
Somethin' you want?!

00:11:23.500 --> 00:11:25.670
Uh, well...

00:11:26.170 --> 00:11:27.920
Oh, it's a police officer!

00:11:46.960 --> 00:11:49.580
Man, I'm so lame.

00:11:52.380 --> 00:11:55.000
Whew, I'm so nervous.

00:11:56.460 --> 00:11:58.330
Excuse me!

00:11:58.710 --> 00:12:02.130
I'm Eiko Tsukimi, and I'm here
for the recording session...

00:12:03.080 --> 00:12:04.500
Um...

00:12:08.580 --> 00:12:09.790
Pleased to meet you!

00:12:09.790 --> 00:12:12.420
I'm Eiko Tsukimi, stage name EIKO.

00:12:12.420 --> 00:12:13.830
I look forward to working together!

00:12:14.830 --> 00:12:16.250
Steve Kido...

00:12:16.250 --> 00:12:19.580
<b>Kuriya's Delicious</b>

00:12:16.250 --> 00:12:19.580
<b>Delectable</b>

00:12:16.250 --> 00:12:19.580
<b>Pickled Bamboo Shoots</b>

00:12:17.170 --> 00:12:19.580
the world's top straight-shooting hunk of a DJ.

00:12:19.920 --> 00:12:21.630
Oh, want a bamboo shoot?

00:12:21.630 --> 00:12:23.420
Uh, I'm all right.

00:12:23.920 --> 00:12:27.250
Still, you can't beat bamboo shoots in the studio.

00:12:28.040 --> 00:12:29.250
Here's my card.

00:12:29.250 --> 00:12:31.330
<i>I feel like I know him from somewhere...</i>

00:12:31.750 --> 00:12:33.080
Thank yo-

00:12:34.500 --> 00:12:36.460
<i>Steve Kido...</i>

00:12:36.670 --> 00:12:40.420
<i>That Japanese artist who has DJ'ed in LA and Ibiza?</i>

00:12:40.580 --> 00:12:44.540
<i>Three years ago at Summer Sonia
he flung cakes at the crowd.</i>

00:12:44.960 --> 00:12:46.170
<i>Is it really him?!</i>

00:12:46.380 --> 00:12:48.000
Call me Kid.

00:12:48.290 --> 00:12:49.460
That's what everybody calls me.

00:12:49.920 --> 00:12:51.170
"Kid," you say...

00:12:51.170 --> 00:12:52.670
Are you THAT Kid?

00:12:53.040 --> 00:12:54.290
Which Kid?

00:12:54.290 --> 00:12:56.040
There are many Kids, you know.

00:12:56.330 --> 00:12:59.540
Like the phantom thief, the martial artist, a medical kit...

00:13:03.210 --> 00:13:04.790
Oh, go ahead and quip back.

00:13:04.790 --> 00:13:06.580
<i>What a pain in the butt...</i>

00:13:06.580 --> 00:13:09.330
So, your manager Kongming...

00:13:09.710 --> 00:13:10.960
He's amusing.

00:13:10.960 --> 00:13:12.210
Where'd you find him?

00:13:12.750 --> 00:13:14.750
Um, somewhere around town.

00:13:15.130 --> 00:13:19.000
So, you think maybe he's the real Kongming?

00:13:19.500 --> 00:13:20.710
Who knows?

00:13:20.710 --> 00:13:22.790
I haven't seen the real one, after all.

00:13:23.170 --> 00:13:25.210
You talked with Kongming, Kid?

00:13:25.830 --> 00:13:27.290
We've made a wager.

00:13:27.790 --> 00:13:30.540
If you can make a song I'm satisfied with,
there's no charge.

00:13:30.920 --> 00:13:34.000
But if you can't, Kongming will become my tactician.

00:13:34.250 --> 00:13:36.750
<i>What?! That's news to me!</i>

00:13:37.250 --> 00:13:39.420
<i>Why would you promise that, Kongming?</i>

00:13:40.130 --> 00:13:43.750
Out of curiosity, how much would you normally charge?

00:13:44.080 --> 00:13:46.790
For an urgent request with a two-week timeframe...

00:13:46.790 --> 00:13:48.000
about 10 million yen.

00:13:48.000 --> 00:13:49.330
<i>Ten mil-</i>

00:13:49.330 --> 00:13:50.670
<i>No way we could pay that!</i>

00:13:51.000 --> 00:13:54.040
Aw, but I'm not feeling very motivated.

00:13:54.040 --> 00:13:55.250
You can head home for today.

00:13:55.250 --> 00:13:56.250
Huh?!

00:13:56.250 --> 00:13:58.460
<i>Seriously? We're already pressed for time.</i>

00:13:58.750 --> 00:14:01.540
Please! We don't have very much time.

00:14:01.540 --> 00:14:03.380
Can we get started now?

00:14:04.750 --> 00:14:06.380
Well, I'm not really in the mood...

00:14:07.750 --> 00:14:11.210
<b>Puri Pudding</b>

00:14:07.750 --> 00:14:11.210
<b>Jumbo Value-Size</b>

00:14:08.330 --> 00:14:09.790
Jumbo Value-Size Puri Pudding!

00:14:12.710 --> 00:14:13.960
Can I have both?

00:14:13.960 --> 00:14:16.210
Ah, sure! Go right ahead!

00:14:16.500 --> 00:14:17.710
Well then...

00:14:18.420 --> 00:14:19.920
Bamboo-shoot pudding...

00:14:25.670 --> 00:14:28.670
Eating bamboo-shoot pudding
in the studio is the best!

00:14:28.670 --> 00:14:30.580
<i>Some taste in food...</i>

00:14:31.630 --> 00:14:32.830
All right...

00:14:33.170 --> 00:14:34.500
Okay, let's do this.

00:14:35.000 --> 00:14:36.500
I'll at least earn those puddings.

00:14:36.500 --> 00:14:38.040
Please and thank you!

00:14:38.670 --> 00:14:40.670
<i>This did come in handy, Kongming!</i>

00:14:42.000 --> 00:14:43.580
I heard the song you made.

00:14:44.040 --> 00:14:45.250
Good stuff.

00:14:45.250 --> 00:14:46.710
Thank you!

00:14:47.210 --> 00:14:48.420
Wanna make a bet?

00:14:49.460 --> 00:14:53.710
Sing something by your adored Maria Diesel
and get me motivated to work.

00:14:54.000 --> 00:14:57.000
If you do, I'll more than just earn those puddings.

00:14:57.290 --> 00:14:59.130
<i>Maria Diesel...</i>

00:14:59.130 --> 00:15:00.580
<i>My idol...</i>

00:15:01.710 --> 00:15:05.330
<i>She's the one who sparked my goal
of becoming a singer.</i>

00:15:06.000 --> 00:15:07.000
I'll do it!

00:15:07.000 --> 00:15:08.080
Let me show what I've got!

00:15:10.710 --> 00:15:12.000
As for the song...

00:15:16.500 --> 00:15:18.830
<i>"I'm still alive today..."</i>

00:15:19.460 --> 00:15:23.170
<i>If I run away now,
Summer Sonia will be a distant dream.</i>

00:15:24.130 --> 00:15:27.420
<i>It will be okay.
I've sang this song hundreds of times before!</i>

00:15:28.080 --> 00:15:29.290
<i>All right!</i>

00:15:35.670 --> 00:15:36.880
How was that?

00:15:37.540 --> 00:15:38.750
You're really good.

00:15:38.920 --> 00:15:40.250
Thank you!

00:15:40.580 --> 00:15:42.080
Your range is excellent.

00:15:42.460 --> 00:15:43.880
You self-taught?

00:15:43.880 --> 00:15:44.880
Yes!

00:15:44.880 --> 00:15:48.920
While Maria Diesel's songs are
like clippings of daily life,

00:15:48.920 --> 00:15:50.960
they also have an almost religious aspect.

00:15:50.960 --> 00:15:53.500
They feature breathing that's like she's praying to God.

00:15:54.000 --> 00:15:55.830
R&B and soul...

00:15:55.830 --> 00:15:59.290
and recently she's crossing over into EDM and house.

00:15:59.710 --> 00:16:02.500
She's always searching for new forms of expression.

00:16:02.750 --> 00:16:03.920
You said it!

00:16:03.920 --> 00:16:07.080
I love both her older songs and her new stuff.

00:16:07.080 --> 00:16:10.290
Yeah, I could tell as much after hearing you sing.

00:16:10.880 --> 00:16:12.460
So, does that mean you're motivated to-

00:16:12.460 --> 00:16:13.670
Listen...

00:16:14.250 --> 00:16:16.210
You're missing your own voice.

00:16:16.380 --> 00:16:17.380
Huh?

00:16:18.790 --> 00:16:20.460
Ya Boy Kongming!

00:16:18.790 --> 00:16:19.080
<b><i>ya</i></b>

00:16:19.080 --> 00:16:19.630
<b><i>ya Boy</i></b>

00:16:19.630 --> 00:16:19.830
<b><i>ya Boy KONG</i></b>

00:16:19.830 --> 00:16:21.960
<b><i>ya Boy KONGMING!</i></b>

00:16:23.790 --> 00:16:24.790
Kongming...

00:16:24.790 --> 00:16:26.790
You sure it's okay not to be there with Eiko?

00:16:27.130 --> 00:16:29.750
I've provided Eiko with a plan.

00:16:29.750 --> 00:16:31.290
You needn't worry.

00:16:31.380 --> 00:16:34.500
Like how you gave Zhao Yun,
who was escorting Liu Bei, stratagems?

00:16:34.500 --> 00:16:35.830
I know that one!

00:16:35.830 --> 00:16:37.460
But this is no game.

00:16:37.710 --> 00:16:39.960
Can she beat out her rival Azalea using that?

00:16:40.880 --> 00:16:42.000
A stone...

00:16:42.540 --> 00:16:44.790
when polished becomes a gem.

00:16:45.290 --> 00:16:49.250
Eiko will surely overcome this trial.

00:16:50.250 --> 00:16:52.960
That is what I believe.

00:16:54.250 --> 00:16:55.920
You're missing your own voice.

00:16:56.130 --> 00:16:57.790
I can't see you in your singing.

00:16:57.790 --> 00:16:59.500
Er, what does that-

00:16:59.500 --> 00:17:02.290
Don't come back until you're able to find yourself.

00:17:02.290 --> 00:17:03.670
Oh, come on!

00:17:03.670 --> 00:17:06.290
We need to finish the song within two weeks!

00:17:07.920 --> 00:17:09.130
Well...

00:17:10.420 --> 00:17:11.580
you better hurry.

00:17:15.250 --> 00:17:16.580
I won't run from the situation

00:17:16.580 --> 00:17:17.790
New generation

00:17:17.790 --> 00:17:19.000
New nation

00:17:19.330 --> 00:17:20.540
I'll show ya tonight

00:17:20.540 --> 00:17:23.500
<b>loser</b>

00:17:20.540 --> 00:17:23.500
<b>I</b>

00:17:20.540 --> 00:17:23.500
<b>new nation                           new generation</b>

00:17:21.000 --> 00:17:23.040
The loser's got no human rights!

00:17:23.830 --> 00:17:25.080
Ah, it's crap!

00:17:25.080 --> 00:17:27.330
I'm not gonna beat Sekitoba with this stuff.

00:17:33.210 --> 00:17:36.420
<i>Sekitoba's gotten even better than he was back then.</i>

00:17:36.750 --> 00:17:38.290
<i>I'm gonna need punchier,</i>

00:17:38.290 --> 00:17:40.630
<i>more powerful lyrics to win this thing.</i>

00:17:38.290 --> 00:17:40.130
<b>loser</b>

00:17:38.290 --> 00:17:40.130
<b>I</b>

00:17:38.290 --> 00:17:40.130
<b>new nation                           new generation</b>

00:17:42.040 --> 00:17:46.210
Apparent strength is not, in fact, true strength.

00:17:47.210 --> 00:17:49.290
What the hell's that mean?!

00:17:49.500 --> 00:17:50.830
He pisses me off!

00:17:51.080 --> 00:17:52.580
He pisses me off!

00:17:52.580 --> 00:17:54.380
Who even talks like that?

00:17:54.380 --> 00:17:57.250
I know I have a long way to go, but still!

00:17:59.630 --> 00:18:02.460
Well, I do need to finish my song...

00:18:02.790 --> 00:18:05.710
How am I supposed to find myself anyway?

00:18:07.960 --> 00:18:13.420
<b>Application for Permission for Public Road Usage</b>

00:18:07.960 --> 00:18:13.420
<b>Name    Eiko Tsukimi</b>

00:18:07.960 --> 00:18:13.420
<b>Intended Usage of Road                 Live performance</b>

00:18:07.960 --> 00:18:13.420
<b>Place or Section                 Shibuya Hachiko Square thru Center Gai</b>

00:18:08.710 --> 00:18:10.710
That stratagem I got from Kongming...

00:18:10.710 --> 00:18:13.250
A public-road-usage permit...

00:18:13.920 --> 00:18:16.130
Does he want me to perform on the street?

00:18:26.830 --> 00:18:29.880
<i>Whoa, lots of people are out performing.</i>

00:18:29.960 --> 00:18:33.080
<i>Besides, I've never actually sung on the street before.</i>

00:18:34.250 --> 00:18:36.960
<i>All the good spots are already taken.</i>

00:18:39.630 --> 00:18:41.380
<i>Where should I set up?</i>

00:18:44.920 --> 00:18:46.250
<i>That song...</i>

00:18:49.670 --> 00:18:53.080
Everything seemed to be alright

00:18:54.710 --> 00:18:59.130
Cause you gave me whispers of love all night

00:18:59.830 --> 00:19:01.170
<i>She's great!</i>

00:19:01.170 --> 00:19:03.880
<i>But rather than just attempting to perform it well,</i>

00:19:01.880 --> 00:19:05.290
But I'm alone tonight

00:19:03.880 --> 00:19:06.420
<i>it's her raw desire to sing that really hits you.</i>

00:19:06.210 --> 00:19:10.500
And I don't know how to stop heaving sighs

00:19:09.290 --> 00:19:10.500
Excuse me!

00:19:10.500 --> 00:19:11.710
Can I have a word?

00:19:12.000 --> 00:19:13.380
Uh, okay.

00:19:13.630 --> 00:19:15.880
Do you have public-road-usage permit?

00:19:16.710 --> 00:19:18.500
No, I don't.

00:19:18.500 --> 00:19:20.630
That won't do; you need to get permission.

00:19:21.130 --> 00:19:21.750
What's your name? Do you have ID?

00:19:21.750 --> 00:19:23.330
What should I do?
What's your name? Do you have ID?<b></b>

00:19:23.830 --> 00:19:26.210
Uh, well, my license is...

00:19:26.210 --> 00:19:28.960
Sorry! I overslept!

00:19:30.000 --> 00:19:32.000
I brought the permit!

00:19:32.000 --> 00:19:33.670
Sorry to keep you waiting.

00:19:33.880 --> 00:19:34.880
You know her?

00:19:34.880 --> 00:19:36.080
Yes!

00:19:36.670 --> 00:19:39.380
Well, there's no issue if you have permission.

00:19:39.580 --> 00:19:41.790
But take care not to play too loudly.

00:19:42.040 --> 00:19:44.080
Yes, ma'am! Thanks for your hard work!

00:19:45.380 --> 00:19:47.130
Uh, who are you?

00:19:47.130 --> 00:19:49.710
Aw, sorry! Did I trouble you?

00:19:49.710 --> 00:19:51.880
I wanted to hear more of your singing is all!

00:19:52.750 --> 00:19:54.750
Nope, you saved my skin.

00:19:54.750 --> 00:19:55.750
Thanks.

00:19:55.750 --> 00:19:57.040
Glad to hear it.

00:19:57.040 --> 00:19:58.330
I was in a big panic.

00:19:58.330 --> 00:19:59.750
Why would you be?

00:20:00.750 --> 00:20:02.130
You gonna perform out here, too?

00:20:02.130 --> 00:20:06.040
Well, that's the plan, but this is
my first time and I've got cold feet.

00:20:07.080 --> 00:20:09.710
Those police officers are still looking this way.

00:20:09.710 --> 00:20:11.290
Seems they're still skeptical.

00:20:12.330 --> 00:20:14.380
Hey, you play guitar, right?

00:20:16.170 --> 00:20:18.290
Wanna play together, then?

00:20:18.290 --> 00:20:19.290
Okay?

00:20:20.540 --> 00:20:21.540
Okay!

00:20:22.170 --> 00:20:23.420
What song should we do?

00:20:23.420 --> 00:20:26.540
Oh, want to keep going with "I'm still alive today"?

00:20:26.670 --> 00:20:28.380
Sounds good. You wanna sing?

00:20:28.380 --> 00:20:30.880
Nah, I wanna hear you sing.

00:20:31.080 --> 00:20:33.080
Okay, well then...

00:20:48.040 --> 00:20:51.670
Everything seemed to be alright

00:20:53.040 --> 00:20:57.580
Cause you gave me whispers of love all night

00:21:00.170 --> 00:21:03.500
But I'm alone tonight

00:21:04.380 --> 00:21:08.750
And I don't know how to stop heaving sighs

00:21:08.210 --> 00:21:10.380
You've been divining for quite a while now.

00:21:10.380 --> 00:21:11.630
You get a bad sign?

00:21:10.500 --> 00:21:13.170
I just wanna get you out of my mind

00:21:11.630 --> 00:21:12.830
No...

00:21:12.830 --> 00:21:15.540
Will this sign turn up good luck or bad?

00:21:13.170 --> 00:21:15.920
You don't know how much I love you

00:21:15.540 --> 00:21:17.250
I still do not know.

00:21:16.500 --> 00:21:20.420
But you don't wanna be with me any more

00:21:17.250 --> 00:21:20.580
That said, fate is full of ups and downs.

00:21:20.920 --> 00:21:23.750
I'm still alive today

00:21:23.750 --> 00:21:26.540
You are so far away

00:21:26.540 --> 00:21:32.080
Even though you have broken my heart, baby

00:21:32.290 --> 00:21:35.040
I'm still alive today

00:21:35.040 --> 00:21:37.830
And miss you all day

00:21:37.830 --> 00:21:43.380
I just thought I could not live without you

00:21:39.750 --> 00:21:43.040
Ah, that was a blast!

00:21:43.710 --> 00:21:45.290
Wanna perform together tomorrow, too?

00:21:45.420 --> 00:21:46.960
Sounds good, I'm in!

00:21:47.290 --> 00:21:48.960
I wanna hear you sing, too.

00:21:51.460 --> 00:21:53.500
By the way, I'm Eiko Tsukimi.

00:21:53.500 --> 00:21:54.710
Call me Eiko.

00:21:55.080 --> 00:21:56.290
Well then...

00:21:56.420 --> 00:21:57.920
call me Nanami.

00:21:58.210 --> 00:22:00.130
Nice to know you, Nanamin!

00:22:02.500 --> 00:22:03.880
A worthy rival...

00:22:05.130 --> 00:22:08.130
To think the sworn friends sign has appeared...

00:22:11.500 --> 00:22:12.040
<b>Plan for Peace Throughout the World</b>

00:22:12.040 --> 00:22:13.080
<b>Plan for Peace Throughout the World, Vol. 1</b>

